    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a high-variance schedule today, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 76.04 efficiency score remains our top play despite a daunting matchup against Gerrit Cole. While the opposing xERA of 3.46 suggests a difficult outing, the 16% park factor boost and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s favorable platoon split effectively neutralize the talent gap. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** provides excellent value at 74.56; he benefits from a more favorable matchup against Kyle Bradish, and his placement in the #3 slot provides the RBI opportunities necessary to remain a cornerstone of our daily production.\n\nOur most critical bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 38.21 score\u2014just shy of our 40-point threshold for active duty. While **Nasim Nunez** is a high-upside asset due to his elite sprint speed and SB potential, the optimizer ultimately penalized him for the extreme difficulty of facing Jacob deGrom and his poor #9 lineup position. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** continues to be a sneaky catalyst, earning a strong 63.14 score thanks to a favorable #1 batting spot and a soft matchup against G. Holmes. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Luis Lara**, whose #9 spot in the order suppresses his ceiling to 41.15, leaving him as a borderline play. \n\nStrategic risks for the day are concentrated in our \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Because we are projecting batting orders for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Coby Mayo**, any late-breaking shifts in the batting order could necessitate immediate adjustments to our expected efficiency scores. Notably, **Coby Mayo** is trending downward at 46.68; facing an elite arm like Cole while relegated to the #5 spot makes him our most vulnerable starter. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as their absence keeps our depth thin while we await the return of reinforcements like **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Liam Hicks**.",
